-- ownership: a summary past the width cap (`ownership-checker.md` §16.7).
-- `w8` places its argument at 256 result paths, four times the cap, so its
-- summary is coarsened — the paths cut and ended with `⋆`, each entry
-- approximate — not dropped to the pessimistic one. A caller still sees
-- that the result may hold the argument: extending a place of it while
-- the argument is read later is rejected, `call`, approximate.
w1 x = ( x, x )


w2 x = w1 (w1 x)


w4 x = w2 (w2 x)


w8 x = w4 (w4 x)


pub wide : List Int → Int
wide xs =
    t = w8 xs
    ys = [ …t.0.0.0.0.0.0.0.0, 1 ]
    List.length ys + List.length xs
